# PX4 parameters for a real vehicle flying this stack (roadmap item 27 block 1,
# specification K34; docs/px4_parameters.md). QGroundControl's parameter file
# format: vehicle id, component id, name, value, type (6 float, 9 int32).
# Loaded with QGroundControl or `param import` on the vehicle; the simulation
# keeps its own set (scripts/px4_parameter_runtime.sh). An example to start
# from, not a tuning: the battery, the fence's sizes and the frame's own
# parameters are this airframe's to set.
#
# Safety, as PX4 ships it: the power supply is checked (the simulation turns
# the check off, CBRK_SUPPLY_CHK 894281), the loss of the radio and of the
# ground station act by PX4's defaults, and the stack does not override them.
1	1	CBRK_SUPPLY_CHK	0	6
1	1	NAV_RCL_ACT	2	6
1	1	NAV_DLL_ACT	0	6
1	1	COM_RC_IN_MODE	0	6
1	1	COM_RCL_EXCEPT	0	6
# The offboard stream: lost after a second, then the failsafe's action.
1	1	COM_OF_LOSS_T	1.0	9
1	1	COM_OBL_RC_ACT	0	6
# Landed and disarmed: two seconds after the landing is detected (the end of
# every mission, specification K30).
1	1	COM_DISARM_LAND	2.0	9
1	1	COM_KILL_DISARM	5.0	9
# The geofence, an example the size of the simulated location (about 300 m
# across, 40 m high): hold at the fence. PX4 evaluates it on a global
# position; in a GNSS-denied flight it has none and the fence is not
# evaluated, which leaves the mission's own flight envelope as the bound.
1	1	GF_ACTION	2	6
1	1	GF_MAX_HOR_DIST	150.0	9
1	1	GF_MAX_VER_DIST	40.0	9
# The battery: its cells and capacity give PX4 a time left, which the
# mission's return weighs against the way home (specification K32).
1	1	BAT1_N_CELLS	4	6
1	1	BAT1_CAPACITY	5000.0	9
1	1	BAT_LOW_THR	0.15	9
1	1	BAT_CRIT_THR	0.07	9
1	1	COM_LOW_BAT_ACT	3	6
# The estimator: the camera (or lidar) estimator's external odometry for
# position, velocity, height and heading, no GNSS, no magnetometer, the
# external height as the reference (the simulation's visual_inertial and
# lidar_inertial profiles).
1	1	EKF2_GPS_CTRL	0	6
1	1	EKF2_EV_CTRL	15	6
1	1	EKF2_HGT_REF	3	6
1	1	EKF2_MAG_TYPE	5	6
1	1	EKF2_EV_DELAY	0.0	9
1	1	EKF2_EV_NOISE_MD	0	6
